@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-general`

-- SPECIAL CONDITIONS (src:700-977) and the closing notice (src:982-983), in the order
-- printed, under the three headings that say which coverage part each reaches:
--   * CGL part only: the Completed Operations Hazard and Products Hazard Exclusion Clause;
--   * P&CO part only: the Business Risk Exclusion, the Claims Made Basis Endorsement and
--     the Claim Series Clause (all three stand under the P&CO heading at src:716, before
--     the next heading at src:781; NOTES.md, fork F18);
--   * all coverage parts: the twelve clauses from the Asbestos Exclusion to the War and
--     Terrorism Exclusion.
-- The preamble makes every one of them part of the Policy and lets each "supersede any
-- other similar" clause. Which clause is "similar" to which is read clause by clause:
-- the Combined Single Limit Endorsement rewrites III (fork F10), and the Ultimate Net Loss
-- Clause restates the Supplementary Payments with Singapore dollar caps (fork F4).

§ `SPECIAL CONDITIONS`
-- src:700 | SPECIAL CONDITIONS
-- src:702 | The following Exclusions/Exceptions/Clauses/Warranties shall form part of the Policy and shall supersede any other similar
-- src:703 | Exclusions/Exceptions/Clauses/Warranties in the Policy.

§§ `Applicable to Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part Only`
-- src:706 | Applicable to Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part Only

§§§ `COMPLETED OPERATIONS HAZARD AND PRODUCTS HAZARD EXCLUSION CLAUSE`

-- "directly or indirectly arising out of or relating to or resulting from" the two hazards:
-- read as harm within either hazard as the definitions define them (NOTES.md, fork F19).
-- Its effect is that the CGL part covers premises and operations only, which leaves the
-- CGL part's own products and completed operations aggregates (src:512-514, 535-536) with
-- nothing to apply to (finding X3).
-- src:708 | COMPLETED OPERATIONS HAZARD AND PRODUCTS HAZARD EXCLUSION CLAUSE
-- src:710 | It is hereby declared and agreed that notwithstanding anything stated herein to the contrary, the Comprehensive General
-- src:711 | Liability Insurance Coverage Part of this Policy does not apply to any losses or damage including any kind of consequential
-- src:712 | economic loss, directly or indirectly arising out of or relating to or resulting from completed operations hazard and/or
-- src:713 | products hazard.
@ref src:710-713
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Completed Operations Hazard and Products Hazard Exclusion Clause applies` claim MEANS
        `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim
    OR  `the harm is included within the products hazard` claim

§§ `Applicable to Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part Only`
-- src:716 | Applicable to Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part Only

§§§ `BUSINESS RISK EXCLUSION`

-- src:718 | BUSINESS RISK EXCLUSION
-- src:720 | It is agreed that this insurance does not apply to bodily injury or property damage resulting from the failure of the named
-- src:721 | insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured, to perform the function or to serve the purpose
-- src:722 | intended by the named insured, if such failure is due to a mistake or deficiency in any design, formula, plan, specifications,
-- src:723 | advertising material or printed instructions prepared or developed by any insured; but this exclusion does not apply to bodily
-- src:724 | injury or property damage resulting from the active malfunctioning of such products or work.
@ref src:720-724
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Business Risk Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm results from the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to perform the function or to serve the purpose intended by the named insured`
    AND `for` claim `,` `that failure is due to a mistake or deficiency in a design, formula, plan, specifications, advertising material or printed instructions prepared or developed by an insured`
    AND NOT "but" ... `for` claim `,` `the harm results from the active malfunctioning of those products or that work`

§§§ `CLAIMS MADE BASIS ENDORSEMENT`

-- Clause 1 adds four conditions to the P&CO insuring agreement. It does NOT displace the
-- definitions of "bodily injury" and "property damage", which still require the harm to
-- occur during the policy period; read together, the harm must occur AND the claim be
-- made in the same period (NOTES.md, fork F20; finding X1).
-- src:727 | CLAIMS MADE BASIS ENDORSEMENT
-- src:729 | It is understood and agreed that
-- src:731 | 1. Coverage hereunder shall apply only in respect of claim(s) made against any insured during the policy period of this
-- src:732 | insurance stated in the declarations solely by reason of bodily injury or property damage which is included within the
-- src:733 | completed operations hazard or the products hazard sustained after the Retroactive Date stated below and of which
-- src:734 | immediate notice has been given in accordance with the Conditions herein provided always that at the effective date of
-- src:735 | this policy any Insured did not know or could not reasonably have foreseen that such bodily injury or property damage
-- src:736 | might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit.
-- src:754 | Retroactive Date: As stated in the Policy Schedule

-- The date the claim is made, or deemed made, for clause 1:
--   * a claim in a Claim Series Event: the series date (Claim Series Clause 3);
--   * otherwise the claim's own date, and clause 4's deeming as a second route.
@ref src:731-732, 746-750, 768-772
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 1 — the claim is made, or deemed made, during the policy period` policy claim MEANS
    IF   `Claim Series — the claim belongs to a Claim Series Event` claim
    THEN `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` (`Claim Series 3 — the date of claims-made of the series` claim)
    ELSE    `the claim's own date falls in the policy period` policy claim
         OR `Claims Made Basis 4 — the claim is deemed made during the policy period` policy claim

@ref src:731-732
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim's own date falls in the policy period` policy claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` d

-- "Retroactive Date: As stated in the Policy Schedule". Where the schedule states none, a
-- rule that needs it is declined by name.
@ref src:754
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
GIVETH A DATE
`the Retroactive Date of` policy MEANS
    `the date` (policy's `the retroactive date stated in the policy schedule`) `, or else` `the Retroactive Date is not in the record`

@ref src:754
GIVETH A DATE
`the Retroactive Date is not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Retroactive Date stated in the Policy Schedule is not in the record"

-- "sustained after the Retroactive Date": strictly after (NOTES.md, fork F21).
@ref src:733
GIVEN d      IS A DATE
      policy IS A `The policy as declared`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 1 — the harm, dated` d `, is sustained after the Retroactive Date of` policy MEANS
    d GREATER THAN `the Retroactive Date of` policy

@ref src:733-734
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 1 — immediate notice has been given` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `immediate notice of the harm has been given in accordance with the Conditions`

-- "provided always that at the effective date of this policy any Insured did not know or
-- could not reasonably have foreseen ...". Read as written: the proviso holds if no
-- insured knew, OR if it could not reasonably have been foreseen; it fails only where an
-- insured both knew and could have foreseen (NOTES.md, fork F22; finding X6).
@ref src:734-736
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 1 — the proviso on knowledge at the effective date holds` claim MEANS
        NOT `for` claim `,` `at the effective date of the policy an insured knew that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`
    OR  NOT `for` claim `,` `at the effective date of the policy an insured could reasonably have foreseen that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`

-- The reading the insurer would put forward, kept for comparison and for the finding: the
-- proviso holds only if an insured neither knew nor could reasonably have foreseen.
@ref src:734-736
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 1 — the proviso on knowledge, read as "neither knew nor could have foreseen"` claim MEANS
        NOT `for` claim `,` `at the effective date of the policy an insured knew that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`
    AND NOT `for` claim `,` `at the effective date of the policy an insured could reasonably have foreseen that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`

-- Clause 2: each claimant's claim is that claimant's alone. Encoded by the shape: one claim
-- record is one claimant's claim, and its date is its own.
-- src:738 | 2. A claim made by a person, firm or corporation against any insured during the period of Insurance stated in the
-- src:739 | declarations, arising out of an occurrence, shall be deemed to have been so made solely on such claimant's behalf,
-- src:740 | and shall in no event be deemed a notice or claim made by any other person, firm or corporation against any insured,
-- src:741 | arising out of the same accident, within the terms of the coverage afforded by this policy.

-- src:743 | 3. No coverage shall be deemed afforded hereunder for any claim for such bodily injury or property damage which has or
-- src:744 | is alleged to have been caused to any extent or degree, directly or indirectly prior to the Retroactive Date of this policy.
@ref src:743-744
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 3 — the harm was caused before the Retroactive Date` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the harm has been, or is alleged to have been, caused to any extent or degree, directly or indirectly, before the Retroactive Date`

-- Clause 4 reaches circumstances "by reason of the named insured's products" only: not
-- completed operations (finding X7). First awareness and the written notice must both fall
-- in the policy period.
-- src:746 | 4. If during the policy period any Insured shall first become aware of any circumstances which may subsequently give
-- src:747 | rise to a claim against any insured by reason of the named insured's products for which coverage would be afforded
-- src:748 | hereunder and if any insured shall during the policy period herein give written notice to the Company of such
-- src:749 | circumstances, any claim that may subsequently be made against any insured arising out of such products shall be
-- src:750 | deemed for the purpose of this insurance to have been made during the policy period stated in the declarations. Any
-- src:751 | insured shall cooperate fully with the Company as provided in the Conditions, and any investigation conducted by the
-- src:752 | Company or its representatives shall be subject to the terms set forth in this insurance.
@ref src:746-750
GIVEN policy IS A `The policy as declared`
      claim  IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claims Made Basis 4 — the claim is deemed made during the policy period` policy claim MEANS
        `the harm arises out of the named insured's products` claim
    AND `for` claim `,` `the claim arises out of the named insured's products to which the notified circumstances relate`
    AND `the date falls in the policy period` (claim's `the date an insured first became aware of circumstances which may give rise to the claim`)
    AND `the date falls in the policy period` (claim's `the date written notice of those circumstances was given to the Company`)
    WHERE
        `the date falls in the policy period` md MEANS
            CONSIDER md
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d  THEN `it occurs during the policy period of` policy `on` d

§§§ `CLAIM SERIES CLAUSE`

-- src:757 | CLAIM SERIES CLAUSE
-- src:758 | (To be applied in conjunction with the Claims Made Basis Endorsement)
-- src:760 | Notwithstanding anything contained to the contrary herein, it is understood and agreed that:
-- src:762 | 1. ‘A Claim Series Event’ defined below shall be deemed as one whose date of loss shall be determined strictly on the
-- src:763 | basis set out below.
-- src:765 | 2. ‘A Claim Series Event’ means a series of two or more claims arising from one specific common cause which is
-- src:766 | attributable to one design and/or specification and/or formula in products and/or services supplied by one insured.
@ref src:765-766
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claim Series — the claim belongs to a Claim Series Event` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the claim is one of a series of two or more claims arising from one specific common cause attributable to one design, specification or formula in products or services supplied by one insured`

@ref src:762-766
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A `A claim series`
`the claim series of` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the claim series`
    WHEN JUST s  THEN s
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the dates of the Claim Series Event are not in the record`

@ref src:768-773
GIVETH A `A claim series`
`the dates of the Claim Series Event are not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "the dates of the Claim Series Event are not in the record"

-- Clause 3: the series' date of occurrence is the date of its first loss; its date of
-- claims-made is the earlier of the first written advice of the first claim and the
-- written notice to the Company.
-- src:768 | 3. The date of occurrence of such ‘A Claim Series Event’ shall be deemed to be the date that the first loss of the series
-- src:769 | occurred and the date of claims-made of such ‘A Claim Series Event’ shall be deemed to be the date that the insured
-- src:770 | is first advised in writing of the first claim of the Claim Series Event which contributes to the Ultimate Net Loss
-- src:771 | applicable hereto, or the date that the written notice is given by or on behalf of the insured to the Company or any
-- src:772 | authorized agents, whichever is the first. In such circumstances the Company shall include each and every claim
-- src:773 | which could be taken into consideration for the purpose of establishing the date of loss.
@ref src:768
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A DATE
`Claim Series 3 — the date of occurrence of the series` claim MEANS
    (`the claim series of` claim)'s `the date the first loss of the series occurred`

@ref src:768-772
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A DATE
`Claim Series 3 — the date of claims-made of the series` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `the date written notice of the series was given to the Company or an authorized agent`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN s's `the date the insured was first advised in writing of the first claim of the series`
    WHEN JUST notice THEN
        IF   notice LESS THAN s's `the date the insured was first advised in writing of the first claim of the series`
        THEN notice
        ELSE s's `the date the insured was first advised in writing of the first claim of the series`
    WHERE
        s MEANS `the claim series of` claim

-- Clause 4: "within 120 months of the first claim made in writing". Calendar months, the
-- last day of the 120th month included (NOTES.md, fork F23). `add months` clamps the day
-- of the month.
-- src:775 | 4. Claims in ‘A Claim Series Event’ shall only be covered if such claims are made against the insured within 120 months
-- src:776 | of the first claim made in writing against the insured.
@ref src:775-776
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Claim Series 4 — the claim is made within 120 months of the first claim` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date this claim was made is not in the record`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
        d AT MOST `add months` ((`the claim series of` claim)'s `the date the first claim of the series was made in writing against the insured`) 120

@ref src:775
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the date this claim was made is not in the record` MEANS
    REFUSE "the date this claim was made in writing against the insured is not in the record"

§§ `Applicable to All Coverage Parts`
-- src:781 | Applicable to All Coverage Parts

§§§ `ASBESTOS EXCLUSION`

-- src:783 | ASBESTOS EXCLUSION
-- src:785 | Excluding all claims and losses based upon, arising out of, directly or indirectly resulting from or in consequence of, or any
-- src:786 | way involving:
-- src:788 | (a) asbestos, or
-- src:790 | (b) any actual or alleged asbestos related injury or damage involving the use, presence, existence, detection, removal,
-- src:791 | elimination or avoidance of asbestos or exposure or potential exposure to asbestos.
@ref src:785-791
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Asbestos Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        "(a)" ... `for` claim `,` `the claim or loss is based upon, arises out of, directly or indirectly results from, is in consequence of, or in any way involves asbestos`
    OR  "(b)" ... `for` claim `,` `the claim or loss in any way involves actual or alleged asbestos related injury or damage involving the use, presence, existence, detection, removal, elimination or avoidance of asbestos, or exposure or potential exposure to asbestos`

§§§ `COMBINED SINGLE LIMIT ENDORSEMENT`

-- III as amended: one "each occurrence" sum for Coverages A and B together, and one
-- "aggregate" sum for occurrences arising out of the products hazard or the completed
-- operations hazard. It applies where the schedule states those two sums (fork F10).
-- src:794 | COMBINED SINGLE LIMIT ENDORSEMENT
-- src:796 | It is agreed that:
-- src:797 | The provisions of the policy captioned "III Limits of Liability" are amended to read as follows:
-- src:799 | III Limits of Liability
-- src:801 | Regardless of the number of (1) insureds under this policy, (2) persons or organizations who sustain bodily injury or property
-- src:802 | damage, (3) claims made or suits brought on account of bodily injury or property damage the Company's liability is limited
-- src:803 | as follows:
-- src:805 | Coverage A & B－The Company's limit of liability under Coverages A & B, separately or in combination for all damages,
-- src:806 | shall not exceed the sum stated in the Schedule as "each occurrence."
-- src:808 | Subject to the above provision respecting each occurrence:
-- src:809 | The limit of the Company's liability shall not exceed the sum stated in the Schedule as "aggregate," in respect of all
-- src:810 | occurrences arising out of the products hazard and/or completed operations hazard as defined herein.
@ref src:805-810
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Combined Single Limit — the aggregate applies to the occurrence` claim MEANS
        `the harm is included within the products hazard` claim
    OR  `the harm is included within the completed operations hazard` claim

@ref src:805-810
GIVEN `each occurrence` IS A NUMBER
      aggregate         IS A NUMBER
      `already paid`    IS A NUMBER
      claim             IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Combined Single Limit — the cap, each occurrence` `each occurrence` `, aggregate` aggregate `, already paid` `already paid` `, for` claim MEANS
    IF   `Combined Single Limit — the aggregate applies to the occurrence` claim
    THEN min `each occurrence` (max 0 (aggregate MINUS `already paid`))
    ELSE `each occurrence`

-- The one-occurrence rule, stated a third time (src:812-814): msig-cgl-definitions.l4.
-- src:812 | For the purpose of determining the limit of the Company's liability, all bodily injury and property damage arising out of
-- src:813 | continuous or repeated exposure to substantially the same general conditions shall be considered as arising out of one
-- src:814 | occurrence.

§§§ `CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION`

-- src:817 | CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION
-- src:819 | It is hereby understood and agreed that this insurance shall not indemnify the insured in respect of any claim or loss arising
-- src:820 | out of any activities and/or business conducted and/or transacted via the Internet, Intranet, Extranet and/or via the insured’s
-- src:821 | own website, Internet site, web address and/or via the transmission of electronic mail or documents by electronic means.
@ref src:819-821
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Cyber Liability Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the Internet, an Intranet or an Extranet`
    ..  `for` claim `,` `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the insured's own website, Internet site or web address`
    OR  `for` claim `,` `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the transmission of electronic mail or documents by electronic means`

§§§ `DATE RECOGNITION EXCEPTION`

-- src:824 | DATE RECOGNITION EXCEPTION
-- src:826 | There is no insurance under this Policy in respect of any claim of whatsoever nature which arises directly or indirectly from
-- src:827 | or consists of the failure or inability of any
-- src:829 | (a) electronic circuit, microchip, integrated circuit, microprocessor, embedded system, hardware, software, firmware,
-- src:830 | program, computer, data processing equipment, telecommunication equipment or systems, or any similar device
-- src:832 | (b) media or systems used in connection with any of the foregoing
-- src:834 | whether the property of the insured or not, at any time to achieve any or all of the purposes and consequential effects
-- src:835 | intended by the use of any number, symbol or word to denote a date including without limitation, the failure or inability to
-- src:836 | recognise capture save retain or restore and/or correctly to manipulate, interpret, transmit, return, calculate or process any
-- src:837 | date, data, information, command, logic or instruction as a result of
-- src:839 | (i) recognising using or adopting any date, day of the week or period of time, otherwise than as, or other than, the
-- src:840 | true or correct date, day of the week or period of time
-- src:842 | (ii) the operation of any command or logic which has been programmed or incorporated into anything referred to in
-- src:843 | (a) and (b) above.
@ref src:826-843
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Date Recognition Exception applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the claim arises directly or indirectly from, or consists of, the failure or inability of an electronic circuit, microchip, computer, software, telecommunication equipment or similar device, or media or systems used with one, whether the insured's property or not, to achieve a purpose or effect intended by the use of a number, symbol or word to denote a date`
    AND (   "(i)"  ... `for` claim `,` `that failure or inability is a result of recognising, using or adopting a date, day of the week or period of time otherwise than as, or other than, the true or correct one`
         OR "(ii)" ... `for` claim `,` `that failure or inability is a result of the operation of a command or logic programmed or incorporated into such a device, media or system`)

§§§ `ELECTROMAGNETIC FIELDS EXCLUSION`

-- src:846 | ELECTROMAGNETIC FIELDS EXCLUSION
-- src:848 | This Policy shall not indemnify the insured in respect of any loss or liability which arises out of or is contributed to directly or
-- src:849 | indirectly by exposure to magnetic electric or electromagnetic fields or radiation however caused or generated.
@ref src:848-849
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Electromagnetic Fields Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the loss or liability arises out of, or is contributed to directly or indirectly by, exposure to magnetic, electric or electromagnetic fields or radiation, however caused or generated`

§§§ `INSTITUTE RADIOACTIVE CONTAMINATION, CHEMICAL, BIOLOGICAL, BIOCHEMICAL AND ELECTROMAGNETIC WEAPONS EXCLUSION CLAUSE`

-- "This clause shall be paramount": it is an exclusion, so the order in which the answer
-- asks it changes only which reason is reported, never whether there is cover.
-- src:852 | INSTITUTE RADIOACTIVE CONTAMINATION, CHEMICAL, BIOLOGICAL, BIOCHEMICAL AND ELECTROMAGNETIC
-- src:853 | WEAPONS EXCLUSION CLAUSE
-- src:855 | This clause shall be paramount and shall override anything contained in this insurance inconsistent therewith:
-- src:857 | Page 12 of 14
-- src:859 | Revised General Liability Policy Form
-- src:860 | In no case shall this insurance cover loss damage liability or expense directly or indirectly caused by or contributed to by or
-- src:861 | arising from
-- src:863 | (a) ionising radiations from or contamination by radioactivity from any nuclear fuel or from any nuclear waste or from the
-- src:864 | combustion of nuclear fuel
-- src:866 | (b) the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of any nuclear installation, reactor or
-- src:867 | other nuclear assembly or nuclear components thereof
-- src:869 | (c) any weapon or device employing atomic or nuclear fission and/or fusion or other like reaction or radioactive force or
-- src:870 | matter
-- src:872 | (d) the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of any radioactive matter. The
-- src:873 | exclusion in this sub-clause does not extend to radioactive isotopes, other than nuclear fuel, when such isotopes are
-- src:874 | being prepared, carried, stored, or used for commercial, agricultural, medical, scientific or other similar peaceful
-- src:875 | purposes
-- src:877 | (e) any chemical, biological, bio-chemical or electromagnetic weapon.
@ref src:855-877
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Institute Radioactive Contamination Exclusion Clause applies` claim MEANS
        "(a)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from ionising radiations from or contamination by radioactivity from nuclear fuel, nuclear waste or the combustion of nuclear fuel`
    ..  "(b)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of a nuclear installation, reactor or other nuclear assembly or nuclear component`
    ..  "(c)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from a weapon or device employing atomic or nuclear fission or fusion or other like reaction or radioactive force or matter`
    ..  "(d)" ... (    `for` claim `,` `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of radioactive matter`
                   AND NOT `for` claim `,` `that radioactive matter is radioactive isotopes, other than nuclear fuel, being prepared, carried, stored or used for commercial, agricultural, medical, scientific or other similar peaceful purposes`)
    OR  "(e)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from a chemical, biological, bio-chemical or electromagnetic weapon`

§§§ `PROFESSIONAL LIABILITY EXCLUSION`

-- src:880 | PROFESSIONAL LIABILITY EXCLUSION
-- src:882 | This Policy does not apply to or include legal liability arising out of breach of professional duty or wrongful or inadequate
-- src:883 | advice given separately for a fee.
@ref src:882-883
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Professional Liability Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `the liability arises out of breach of professional duty, or wrongful or inadequate advice given separately for a fee`

§§§ `PUNITIVE DAMAGES EXCLUSION`

-- It removes a PART of what is awarded, so it is an amount: the punitive part is left
-- out of the ultimate net loss (msig-cgl-answer.l4) and is never a ground of no cover.
-- src:886 | PUNITIVE DAMAGES EXCLUSION
-- src:888 | This insurance shall not apply to fines, penalties, punitive damages exemplary damages, treble damages, or any other
-- src:889 | damages resulting from the multiplication of compensatory damages.
@ref src:888-889
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Punitive Damages Exclusion takes out` sums MEANS
    sums's `fines, penalties, punitive, exemplary, treble or multiplied damages`

§§§ `SANCTION LIMITATION AND EXCLUSION CLAUSE`

-- "to the extent that": read as reaching the whole claim when the finding is made for it.
-- src:892 | SANCTION LIMITATION AND EXCLUSION CLAUSE
-- src:894 | No Insurer shall be deemed to provide cover and no Insurer shall be liable to pay any claim or provide any benefit hereunder
-- src:895 | to the extent that the provision of such cover, payment of such claim or provision of such benefit would expose that Insurer
-- src:896 | to any sanction, prohibition or restriction under United Nations resolutions or the trade or economic sanctions, laws or
-- src:897 | regulations of the European Union or United Kingdom or United States of America.
@ref src:894-897
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Sanction Limitation and Exclusion Clause applies` claim MEANS
    `for` claim `,` `providing the cover or paying the claim would expose the Company to a sanction, prohibition or restriction under United Nations resolutions or the trade or economic sanctions, laws or regulations of the European Union, the United Kingdom or the United States of America`

§§§ `SISTERSHIP EXCLUSION CLAUSE`

-- Paragraph 1 is a duty with no period ("promptly"); paragraph 2 is its sanction, an
-- exclusion of later harm "arising from the same cause"; paragraph 3 takes the cost of the
-- measures out of the indemnity (msig-cgl-answer.l4 leaves it out of the sums).
-- src:900 | SISTERSHIP EXCLUSION CLAUSE
-- src:902 | It is agreed that:
-- src:904 | 1. In case bodily injury or property damage occurs or is expected to occur, the named insured shall promptly withdraw,
-- src:905 | inspect, repair or replace the named insured's products or work completed by or for the named insured or of any
-- src:906 | property of which such products or work form a part or take all reasonable steps to prevent additional bodily injury or
-- src:907 | property damage arising out of the same or similar conditions where the initial bodily injury or property damage
-- src:908 | occurred.
@ref src:904-908
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Sistership 1 — the named insured withdraws, repairs or replaces, or takes all reasonable steps` MEANS
    PARTY `the named insured`
    MUST  `withdraw, inspect, repair or replace the products or work, or take all reasonable steps to prevent further injury or damage`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:910 | 2. If the named insured fails to take preventive measures mentioned in the above paragraph without any justifiable
-- src:911 | reason, this insurance does not apply to bodily injury or property damage arising from the same cause where the initial
-- src:912 | bodily injury or property damage occurs.
@ref src:910-912
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sistership 2 — the exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `the harm arises from the same cause as an earlier bodily injury or property damage`
    AND `for` claim `,` `after that earlier injury or damage the named insured failed to take the preventive measures the Sistership Exclusion Clause requires`
    AND NOT "without any justifiable reason" ... `for` claim `,` `the named insured had a justifiable reason for that failure`

-- src:914 | 3. The Company shall not indemnify the named insured for any expense, whether or not spent by the named insured, for
-- src:915 | withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement of the products (including the property containing any product as a part
-- src:916 | thereof) or any other expenses spent for other necessary measures taken to prevent any further loss.
@ref src:914-916
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sistership 3 — the expenses not indemnified` sums MEANS
    sums's `expenses of withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement, or of other preventive measures`

§§§ `ULTIMATE NET LOSS CLAUSE`

-- The limits apply to the ultimate net loss: damages plus (b)-(e), which restate
-- Supplementary Payments (a)-(d) with the caps in SINGAPORE DOLLARS (S$250 per bail bond,
-- S$25 per day) where Supplementary Payments print US DOLLARS. This clause opens
-- "Notwithstanding any provision ... contrary" and the preamble makes it supersede a
-- similar clause, so it is taken as operative (NOTES.md, fork F4; finding X4).
-- Clause 1 names coverages "Y" and "Z", which no part of the document defines (finding X9).
-- src:919 | ULTIMATE NET LOSS CLAUSE
-- src:921 | Notwithstanding any provision contained in this Policy which is contrary to the following, it is agreed and understood that:
-- src:923 | 1. In regard of the application of "Limits of Liability", with respect to coverage A, B, Y or Z, or any combination thereof
-- src:924 | limits of liability of the Company shall be only for the ultimate net loss.
-- src:926 | 2. "Ultimate Net Loss" means the total sums defined as follows:
-- src:928 | (a) all sums which the insured shall become legally obligated to pay as damages because of bodily injury or
-- src:929 | property damage to which this insurance applies caused by an occurrence.
@ref src:928-929
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Ultimate Net Loss 2(a)` sums MEANS
        sums's `damages because of bodily injury`
    +   sums's `damages because of property damage`

-- src:931 | (b) all expenses incurred by the Company, all costs taxed against the insured in any suit defended by the
-- src:932 | Company and all interest on the entire amount of any judgement therein which accrues after entry of the
-- src:933 | judgement and before the Company has paid or tendered or deposited in court that part of the judgement which
-- src:934 | does not exceed the limit of the Company's liability thereon.
@ref src:931-934
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Ultimate Net Loss 2(b)` sums MEANS
        sums's `expenses incurred by the Company`
    +   sums's `costs taxed against the insured in a suit defended by the Company`
    +   sums's `interest accruing after entry of judgement and before the Company pays, tenders or deposits its part`

-- src:936 | (c) premiums on appeal bonds required in any such suit, premiums on bonds to release attachments in any such
-- src:937 | suit for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit of liability of this Policy, and the cost of bail bonds
-- src:941 | required of the insured because of accident or traffic law violation arising out of the use of any vehicle to which
-- src:942 | this Policy applies, not to exceed S$250.00 per bail bond, but the Company shall have no obligation to apply for
-- src:943 | or furnish any such bonds.
@ref src:936-943
GIVEN sums  IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Ultimate Net Loss 2(c)` sums rates MEANS
        sums's `premiums on appeal bonds`
    +   sums's `premiums on bonds to release attachments, for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit`
    +   sum (map (GIVEN cost YIELD min cost (250 TIMES rates's `dong per Singapore dollar`)) (sums's `the cost of each bail bond`))

-- src:945 | (d) expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of an accident, for bodily injury to which this
-- src:946 | Policy applies.
@ref src:945-946
GIVEN sums IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Ultimate Net Loss 2(d)` sums MEANS
    sums's `expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of the accident`

-- src:948 | (e) reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request in assisting the Company in the
-- src:949 | investigation or defense of any claim or suit, including actual loss of earnings not to exceed S$25.00 per day.
@ref src:948-949
GIVEN sums  IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Ultimate Net Loss 2(e)` sums rates MEANS
        sums's `reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request, other than loss of earnings`
    +   sum (map (GIVEN earnings YIELD min earnings (25 TIMES rates's `dong per Singapore dollar`)) (sums's `the actual loss of earnings for each day`))

@ref src:923-949
GIVEN sums  IS A `The sums for one occurrence`
      rates IS A `Rates of exchange into dong`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ultimate net loss of` sums `at` rates MEANS
        `Ultimate Net Loss 2(a)` sums
    +   `Ultimate Net Loss 2(b)` sums
    +   `Ultimate Net Loss 2(c)` sums rates
    +   `Ultimate Net Loss 2(d)` sums
    +   `Ultimate Net Loss 2(e)` sums rates

§§§ `WAR & TERRORISM EXCLUSION`

-- The last paragraph moves the burden of proof: once the Company alleges the exclusion,
-- the loss is excluded unless the insured has proved the contrary. The allegation needs
-- no stated ground (finding X10).
-- src:952 | WAR & TERRORISM EXCLUSION
-- src:954 | The insurance by this policy excludes:
-- src:956 | death, disability, loss, damage, destruction, any legal liabilities, cost or expense including consequential loss of whatsoever
-- src:957 | nature, directly or indirectly caused by, resulting from or in connection with any of the following regardless of any other
-- src:958 | cause or event contributing concurrently or in any other sequence to the loss;
-- src:960 | (a) war, invasion, acts of foreign enemies, hostilities or warlike operations (whether war be declared or not), civil war,
-- src:961 | rebellion, revolution, insurrection, civil commotion assuming the proportions of or amounting to an uprising, military or
-- src:962 | usurped power; or
-- src:964 | (b) any act of terrorism including but not limited to
-- src:966 | (i) the use or threat of force, violence and/or
-- src:968 | (ii) harm or damage to life or to property (or the threat of such harm or damage) including, but not limited to, nuclear
-- src:969 | radiation and/or contamination by chemical and/or biological agents,
-- src:971 | by any person(s) or group(s) of persons, committed for political, religious, ideological or similar purposes, express or
-- src:972 | otherwise, and/or to put the public or any section of the public in fear; or
-- src:974 | (c) any action taken in controlling, preventing, suppressing or in any way relating to (a) or (b) above.
-- src:976 | If the Company alleges that by reason of this exclusion, any loss, damage, cost or expense is not covered by this insurance
-- src:977 | the burden of proving the contrary shall be upon the Insured.
@ref src:954-977
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the War and Terrorism Exclusion applies` claim MEANS
    IF   `for` claim `,` `the Company alleges that by reason of the War and Terrorism Exclusion the loss is not covered`
    THEN NOT `for` claim `,` `the insured has proved that the loss is not excluded by the War and Terrorism Exclusion`
    ELSE    "(a)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with war, invasion, acts of foreign enemies, hostilities or warlike operations, civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection, civil commotion assuming the proportions of or amounting to an uprising, or military or usurped power`
         ..  "(b)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with an act of terrorism`
         OR  "(c)" ... `for` claim `,` `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with an action taken in controlling, preventing, suppressing or in any way relating to war or terrorism`

§ `IMPORTANT`

-- A request to the insured, with no consequence attached: named text.
-- src:982 | IMPORTANT—The Insured is requested to read this Policy. If any error or misdescription be found, the Policy
-- src:983 | should be returned to the issuing office for correction.
@ref src:982-983
`the closing notice` MEANS
    "IMPORTANT—The Insured is requested to read this Policy. If any error or misdescription be found, the Policy should be returned to the issuing office for correction."
